    "https://apply.interfolio.com/127840": {
      "title": "HUMA-2023-TSR10-Research Technician",
      "description": "Department: Pompeu Fabra University: Department of Humanities Location: Barcelona Object of the call: A research technician's place is convened to support the research of the Research Group on Social Archaeology and Gender Studies-GRASEG. Tasks: 1. Identification and support of calls for research and dissemination of research. 2. I support the justification and reports of the projects granted. 3. Support in bibliographic databases related to the GRASEG research group. 4. GRASEG Recreation Group social media management. 5. Support for the internationalisation of GRASEG's research through international publications. 6. I support the creation of databases on maintenance activities. 7. I support the work of Castilian primary sources from the 15th–18th centuries. Contract type identification: This is an unfixed permanent contract under RD 32/2021 of 28 December 2021, part-time with a 25-hour weekly dedication. Gross annual payment: EUR 24.876.18 Contract duration: The duration of the contract will be indefinite, not fixed. The start date will be September 2023. Project / segment financing contract 2021 SGR 00926 PID2019-105431GB-I00 Requirements: a) To be in possession of a doctoral degree. b) To be of Spanish nationality or national of one of the Member States of the European Union. In the event of having a nationality outside the Community, the formalisation of the contract will be subject to the obtaining of work permits in accordance with Organic Law 4/2000 of 11 January on the rights and freedoms of foreigners in Spain and their social integration and regulatory implementing provisions. c) To have the functional capacity for the development of the tasks under contract. d) To have the Proficiency in English. e) to have experience in Spanish manuscripts from the 15th–18th centuries. f) To have knowledge and experience in maintenance activities and in the history of food. g) Not to have been separated by disciplinary file from the service of any of the public administrations, nor to be disabled by a firm sentence for the development of public functions. In the case of being a national of another State, it is not incapable or in an equivalent situation, nor has it been subject to disciplinary or equivalent sanctions that would prevent, in its State, in the same terms, access to public jobs. Requirements must be met on the last deadline for submitting applications and must continue to be met on the date of signing the contract. All requirements must be able to be accredited fully at any time in the selective process. Selection criteria: Candidates will be selected by means of a curriculum assessment and, if applicable, by conducting a test and/or interview. The assessment will be as follows: 1.  Academic training: 1 point. 2. Professional experience/Adjustment to the proposed profile: 3 points. 3. Other merits: 1 point. The selection process will consist of evaluating the documentation presented by the candidates based on the selection criteria mentioned, with the possibility, if applicable, of conducting an interview. Selection Commission: PRESIDENT: Ana Delgado Hervas (replacing: Marition Janué) VOWEL 1: Alberto Nodar (replacing: Linda Gale Jones) VOWEL 2: Sandra Montón Subías (replacing: Adriano Orsinger) SECRETARY: Mertixell Ferrer (replacing: Konrad Antczak) Date of publication of the call: 06/07/2023 Application submission deadline: The deadline for submitting applications is 10 working days from the day after the publication of the call on the Humanities Department website: ( https://www.upf.edu/en/web/humanities/open calls ) Requests: The candidates must provide the following documentation: 1. A copy of the academic degree 2. C.V. 3. A letter of motivation 4. DNI/NIE or Passport Copy Applications are submitted via this Interfolio platform. Contact For related queries, address:  seleccio.humanitats@upf.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189077": {
      "title": "HUMA-2026-TSR06: IT Expert – ERC Research Project CoG PHIL-TRAGEN",
      "description": "Department: Pompeu Fabra University: Department of Humanities Location: Barcelona Job Description A vacancy for an IT Specialist position is hereby announced, with an indefinite employment contract as stipulated by Royal Decree (RD) 32/2021 of December 28, 2021, within the framework of the ERC CoG project “PHIL-TRAGEN” (101230032), to provide technical support to the ERC project by facilitating software development, data management, and the maintenance of digital research infrastructure and tools. The ERC project is seeking an IT expert to support the development of its digital research infrastructure. The selected individual will be responsible for designing the database structure, selecting or adapting appropriate software solutions, and collaborating closely with the Principal Investigator and the research team to develop the project’s digital database and an interactive online exhibition. The position requires the ability to translate academic and archival requirements into sustainable digital tools, ensuring their accessibility, usability, and long-term maintenance. Experience with digital humanities projects, research databases, or online exhibitions will be highly valued. The IT expert must be capable of designing a sustainable operational plan for all of the project’s digital outcomes, also taking into account the use of open-source software, compatibility with UPF infrastructure, the UPF open-access repository, and other open-access repositories such as Zenodo. The IT expert will work in close coordination with the project manager to align technical development with project deadlines and reporting requirements. Key Responsibilities: Support the daily administrative and organizational coordination of the ERC project, while providing technical support to the project in accordance with its evolving needs, in close coordination with the Principal Investigator and the Project Manager. Contribute to the development, maintenance, and updating of the project website. Support the design, implementation, and maintenance of the project’s research database. Collaborate on the development and updating of the project’s interactive online exhibition. Assist in the selection, adaptation, and use of digital tools and software solutions necessary for the project’s research and dissemination activities. Ensure the proper organization, accessibility, and sustainability of the project’s digital resources. Provide technical assistance and guidance to team members whenever project activities require it. Support the management and updating of the project's digital communication channels and social media, contributing to dissemination and knowledge transfer activities. Assist in the selection, adaptation, and use of digital tools and software solutions necessary for the project’s research and dissemination activities. Selection Criteria Relevance of technical skills and experience for the project’s needs (50%) Experience in research or academic support environments (20%). Ability to collaborate effectively with researchers and project staff (20%). Flexibility and capacity to adapt technical solutions to evolving project requirements (10%). The minimum score to pass the selection process is: 70 points. The selection committee, if deemed appropriate, may call candidates for an interview or contact the references to clarify aspects of their CV that may help to better evaluate it. Selection Committee The operation of the selection committees will be adjusted to the Regulations on the remote functioning of the sessions of the collegiate bodies of Pompeu Fabra University (Agreement of the Governing Council of December 9, 2020), always holding synchronous sessions. For matters not provided for in these regulations, Law 26/2010, of August 3, on the legal regime and procedure of the public administrations of Catalonia, will apply, without prejudice to the basic rules established in Article 17 of Law 40/2015, of October 1, on the legal regime of the Public Sector. In sessions where candidates must participate, the physical presence of the candidates and, at least, the Secretary of the Committee will be ensured. In the event that a candidate accredits residence outside of Catalonia or justified circumstances prevent their physical presence, they may request the Secretary of the Committee for remote participation. The Secretary may admit this, provided it does not affect the equal participation of the candidates in the performance of the tests and the assessments to be carried out by the Committee. The Selection Committee will conduct interviews with shortlisted candidates as part of the selection process. The Selection Committee will be composed of: PRESIDENT: Libera Pisano (UPF) (substitute: Santiago Zabala, UPF), MEMBER: Bruno Castro Coma (UPF) (substitute: Antonino Firenze, UPF), SECRETARY: Georgios Giannoulis (UPF) (substitute: Albert Fernández, UPF). Processing Unit Humanities Management and Administration Unit Qualifications University degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field, or equivalent professional experience. A Master's degree in Digital Humanities or related fields will be valued. Academic background in philosophy or other humanities disciplines will also be valued, especially if related to the project's thematic area. Experience with digital tools, databases, or software used in research or academic environments, including open-source development software for databases. Experience with the Open Access framework and FAIR principles requirements in EU Horizon projects. Ability to work collaboratively in an interdisciplinary research context. Good communication skills and problem-solving abilities. Excellent command of English; knowledge of German, as well as other languages relevant to the project, will be particularly valued. The requirements must be met by the last day of the application period and must continue to be met on the date the contract is signed. All requirements must be verifiable at any stage of the selection process. Deadline for Submitting Applications The deadline for submitting applications is 15 calendar days from the day following the publication of the call on the Pompeu Fabra University website https://www.upf.edu/web/humanitats/convocatories-obertes Applications are submitted through the Interfolio Platform , at the address that will be published on the Pompeu Fabra University website when the call is made public."
    },
