    "https://apply.interfolio.com/125360": {
      "title": "6 months Research Assistant at Department of Political and Social Sciences - Pompeu Fabra University  (Reference CPIS-PSR-2023-07)",
      "description": "Department: Pompeu Fabra University: Department of Political and Social Sciences Location: Barcelona 6 months Research Assistant at Department of Political and Social Sciences - Pompeu Fabra University  (Reference CPIS-PSR-2023-07) Financing source: Code reference : PREUR02922 EC - CERV - REACT – 101084345. Id Official: 101084345 Project: REACT : Research-Action against Antigypsyism and Anti-Muslim Discrimination: An Intersectional Approach to Deconstruct Institutional Racism in Schools. Research line of the contract: Sociology, ethnic and racial studies, ethnographic methods Functions: The research assistant will work under the supervision of Zenia Hellgren. Tasks: Support in research management Support in data collection and analysis Work cooperatively with the PI, and any other research team members Engage in research project public activities Requirements: PhD in sociology or political science Experience of working with vulnerable populations Documented expertise (publications) in issues related to ethnic diversity and education Good understanding of ethical and emotional issues in fieldwork Experience in project management and coordination Manage multiple activities simultaneously, efficiently and on-time, and be able to meet deadlines. Excellent written and spoken languages skills in English. Catalan and or/Spanish are desirable. Offer publication date: 15/05/2023 Deadline for submission of applications: 31/05/2023 Information about the selection process: h ttps://www.upf.edu/web/politiques/ofertes-de-treball Application process: To apply for this position, candidates send the documentation by interfolio. A letter motivation (1 page) A copy of CV. A copy of your DNI/NIE or Passport Contact: (contact email): zenia.hellgren@upf.edu Selection criteria: Only applications from candidates who fulfill 4 requirements mentioned above will be evaluated: Disciplinary fit with project: 1-5 points; Experience: 1-5 points; Relevant additional skills: 1-5 points The candidate must pass of minimum of 3.5 points for each of selection criteria. The selection committee will decide on the need of an interview with the shortlisted candidates Selection committee: President: Zenia Hellgren Secretary : Dirk Gebhardt Vocal : Lorenzo Gabrielli"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/171236": {
      "title": "CPIS-PSR-2025-20: 12-months Junior Researcher at Universitat Pompeu Fabra, Department of Social and Political Sciences, Barcelona.",
      "description": "Department: Pompeu Fabra University: Department of Political and Social Sciences Location:  Barcelona Research Project: VEARLYDEM. Voting in Early Democracies: The Case of the Spanish Second Republic Funded by Spanish Ministry of Science, Innovation and Universities. Plan Estatal de Investigación Científica, Técnica y de Innovación 2021-2023 Description: The VEARLYDEM project aims to understand the voting patterns during early democratic periods, with the Spanish Second Republic (1931-1939) serving as a case study. One of the goals of the project is to create a quantitative dataset detailing election results at the municipality level during the Spanish Second Republic, the first of its type, and a dataset on legislative speeches. The research team involves partners from different universities, but the PI is located in the UPF Ciutadella Campus (Mercè Rodoreda 24 Building), where the RA will work—online work is also possible upon previous agreement with the PI. Tasks: The RA will develop several tasks, mainly quantitative, to help the team to build the different datasets that are needed for the project. Main tasks: The main tasks for the junior researchers will be: To digitise the information already collected by the research team and input it into a dataset. To clean, categorise and prepare the dataset for the analysis. To contact provincial or local archives to collect the information that is missing—in some circumstances, this may include travelling in-person to the archives. To support the research team with additional clerical or admin duties. Required qualifications for candidate Specific Requirements: 1. Bachelor degree (or equivalent) in any field (preference for social sciences). 2. High level of fluency in written and spoken Spanish and English. 3. Sufficient knowledge of Excel, R and Power Point. 4. Be meticulous and able to work in a quite autonomous way. 5. Attention to detail. Other skills that will be valued: 1. Some knowledge and previous experience with data collection. 2. Some knowledge of the Spanish Second Republic 3. High motivation to learn and adaptability. Terms and conditions of the contract: Type of Contract – Indefinite, by the terms of RD 32/2021 de 28 de desembre de 2021. The estimated start date is the 1st of October 2025. The expected duration of the tasks is 12 months, but it could be extended if both parties agree and there are more tasks to be done. Part-time position: The contract will be for 20 hours per week. Category: Group 3 U. Gross annual salary for a 20h contract is: 16.386,44€, which is a monthly gross salary of 1.181,64 euros. The labour contract includes all the benefits of the Spanish Public Health and Social Security System. Only applications from candidates who fulfil the 4 requirements mentioned above will be evaluated, following these criteria: Experience and skills: 1-5 points Motivation: 1-5 points Selection comittee President: Toni Rodon Substitute: Marc Guinjoan Secretary: Pau Vall-Prat Substitute: Abel Escribà Vocal: Magalí Serra Substitute: Pedro Diz Candidates must pass a minimum of 4 points for each of the selection criteria. The selection committee will consider the possibility of interviewing candidates who pass the minimum score. Deadline to submit applications: 12th of August 2025. Contact: toni.rodon@upf.edu Information about the selection process: https://www.upf.edu/web/politiques/ofertes-de-treball To adress any queries about the technicalities of the process, contact: seleccio.cpis@upf.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194031": {
      "title": "REF CALL: CPIS-PSR-2026-21 One 6-months Senior Researcher at Universitat Pompeu Fabra (UPF), Department of Social and Political Sciences, Barcelona, Catalonia.",
      "description": "Department: Pompeu Fabra University: Department of Political and Social Sciences Location: Barcelona, UPF, Campus Ciutadella  Job title One 6-months Senior Researcher at Universitat Pompeu Fabra (UPF), Department of Social and Political Sciences, Barcelona, Catalonia. REFERENCE CALL : CPIS-PSR-2026-21 Offer publication date: 21st, September 2026 The senior researcher will assist Professor Toni Rodon on the project PRISM (Policing, Representation, Identity and Social Mandate) Deadline to submit applications: 13 th, October, 2026 Financing source: The contract will be funded by the Fundación BBVA—Becas Leonardo de Investigación Científica y Creación Cultural. The Foundation funds the project. Official number reference: PRISM: Policing, Representation, Identity, and Social Mandate . REF LEO26-1-22892. Research Line : Public opinion, social identity, policing, political representation Job description The researcher will offer support on the PRISM project, which pretends to deepen our understanding of the relationship between police legitimacy and identity, considering both citizens’ and law enforcement agents’ identities and examining the role of mediating factors such as political ideology, education and social class. The RA will develop several tasks, mainly quantitative, to support the aforementioned projects. Main tasks : The main tasks for the researcher will be: 1) To clean and analyse aggregate- and individual-level data. 2) To support the PI and the research team designing a survey, and survey experiments. 3) To support the PI and the research team in liaising with the survey company. 4)   To support the research team with additional clerical or admin duties. Requirements: 1. Bachelor’s degree (or equivalent) in any field (preference for social sciences). 2. High level of fluency in written and spoken English. 3. Advanced knowledge of R, and/or Quarto. 4. Experience working on surveys, and survey experiments. 5. Attention to detail. Other skills that will be valued 1. Proficiency in Catalan and Spanish (written and spoken). 2. Experience working on topics related to policing Terms and conditions of the contract Group: 3n Part-time position: The contract is part-time and will be for 17.5 hours per week. Gross annual salary for a 35h contract is: 33407€ approx, which is a monthly gross salary of 2,447€ euros; for a 17.5h contract : gross annual salary: 16 704€ approx Job Location: Barcelona, Catalonia. Type of Contract Indefinite according to the provisions of article 23 bis of the Llei 14/2011, from the 1st of June, of science, technology, and innovation . The labour contract includes all the benefits of the Spanish Public Health and Social Security System. The estimated start date is the 1st November 2026. The expected duration of the tasks is 6 months, but it could be extended if both parties agree and there are more tasks to be done. Selection criteria: Only applications from candidates who fulfil the requirements mentioned above will be evaluated, following these criteria: ● Experience and skills: 1-5 points ● Motivation: 1-5 points Selection committee: ● President: Toni Rodon o Substitute: Martí Rovira ● Secretary: Emanuele Murgolo o Substitute: Marc Sanjaume ● Vocal: Alba Huidobro o Substitute: Alba Lanau Candidates must pass a minimum of 4 points for each of the selection criteria. The selection committee will consider the possibility of interviewing candidates who pass the minimum score. Information on the application process: To apply for this position, interested candidates should send the following documentation: A motivation l etter explaining how the candidates fulfil the requirements mentioned in the job description and why they are interested in this position (1 page) A copy of their CV. A copy of their DNI/NIE or Passport All the information should be sent by Interfolio through the following link: https://apply.interfolio.com/194031 Euraxess Link: https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/jobs/467136 Contact: toni.rodon@upf.edu Information about the selection process : https://www.upf.edu/web/politiques/ofertes-de-treball"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194916": {
      "title": "Full-Time Communication & Knowledge Transfer Manager of the “Maria de Maeztu” Unit of Excellence within the Department of Political and Social Sciences at Universitat Pompeu Fabra (UPF)",
      "description": "Department: Pompeu Fabra University: Department of Political and Social Sciences Location: Barcelona This position is funded by the Grant «Excelencia María de Maeztu» CEX2025-001632-M funded by MICIU/AEI/10.13039/501100011033. The UPF Department of Political and Social Sciences (DPSS) has been officially recognized as a \"María de Maeztu\" Unit of Excellence with the Strategic Program on Equity, Diversity and Democracy (SPEDD) project. This grant is designed to strengthen scientific organization, foster synergies between different UPF research groups, consolidate capacities, promote new lines of research, attract talent, improve international competitiveness and knowledge transfer mechanisms, and promote the training of a new generation of researchers. In order to support SPEDD’s broader mission of social impact, research visibility and outreach efforts, DPSS is hiring a full-time Communication & Knowledge Transfer Manager. Key Responsibilities 1. Design and implement a Strategic Plan for DPSS’s improved global visibility, research impact and public engagement, aligned with SPEDD’s general goal of positioning DPSS as an internationally recognized hub for evidence-based public debate and strategic collaboration. 2. As part of the above-mentioned plan, and in collaboration with the SPEDD team, develop a strategic Science-for-Policy Roadmap focusing on translating research findings into actionable policy recommendations on issues related to democracy, equity, and diversity, including innovative approaches to knowledge transfer and co-production. 3. Strengthen communication efforts as well as partnerships with key local, national and international stakeholders, academic and policy networks, civil society organizations, the media, think tanks, and the broader public. 4. Create and coordinate a dissemination blog with publications and activities produced or generated under the SPEDD framework. 5. Maintain SPEDD’s institutional website, and promote, plan and coordinate strategic activities aimed at improving DPSS’s social media presence, in coordination with UPF’s Communication Office. 6. Promote and coordinate actions to disseminate research outputs and coordinate and supervise the production of audiovisual content linked to SPEDD’s actions, potentially in coordination with an externally-contracted agency/company. 7. Guide DPSS’s researchers in effective communication, knowledge-sharing, sustainability tool integration, and public engagement strategies. 8. Ensure compliance with Open Science principles (data management plans, repositories, FAIR principles) are met in coordination with the UPF Library. 9. Support the smooth implementation of the project, and identify supplementary resources and funding opportunities to maintain and expand SPEDDs’ objectives over time. Conditions 1. Full-time position (35 hrs/week). 2. 4-year contract , aligned with the duration of the Strategic Programme (1 July 2026 – 30 June 2030). Possibility of renewal based on performance and availability of funds. 3. Starting date : Mid-November 2026. 4. Salary : 36.689 Euros gross/year. 5. Workplace : Department of Political and Social Sciences, UPF, Ciutadella Campus, Barcelona. 6. Schedule : split shift. 7. Mode : on-site (with possibility of hybrid work arrangements for 15 hours/week at most). Eligibility Requirements Only applications from candidates fulfilling all of the following requirements will be evaluated: 1. Academic training: At least a Bachelor’s degree in communication, journalism, media studies, Marketing, Digital Media, or social sciences (political science, sociology, public policy, science management, or related disciplines). 2. Languages: advanced knowledge of English; advanced knowledge of Catalan or Spanish (one of the two). To be accredited if the candidate is not a native speaker. 3. Handling of Social Media and knowledge of video and audio editing. 4. Availability to start no later than November 2026. Recruitment Process Total points : 20. ● Phase 1 — Evaluation of application documents: up to 15 points. ● Phase 2 — Personal interview: up to 5 points. The candidates who pass Phase 1 will be invited to an interview, provided they have scored at least 13 points in Phase 1. Selection criteria Phase 1 (up to 15 points) Applications will be evaluated according to the following criteria: Academic training and disciplinary fit with the project (up to 5 points): Relevance of the candidate's academic background to the requirements of the role and thematic scope of SPEDD. Professional experience and fit with the position (up to 5 points): Excellent written and oral communication skills, with the ability to clearly communicate complex research to different audiences. Familiarity with Science-for-Policy and evidence-informed policymaking and experience designing and implementing knowledge-transfer and research-impact strategies. Strong stakeholder-management and networking skills. Experience developing communication strategies across multiple channels, including websites, newsletters, blogs, social media, policy briefs, events, audiovisual content, and media engagement. Experience in public engagement and science communication, preferably in a university, research institution, think tank, NGO, or policy environment. Other merits (up to 5 points): Additional relevant skills and experience, including but not limited to: language proficiency, technical skills, knowledge of university administrative procedures, experience with open science and data management, science communication and stakeholder engagement, and publications or other outputs related to research management. Phase 2 — Personal interview (up to 5 points) The highest-ranked candidates with at least 13 points in Phase 1 will be invited to a personal interview (in person or online). The interview will assess: Communication and interpersonal skills. Knowledge of communication strategies for science dissemination and specific requirements of a María de Maeztu unit. Capacity to coordinate diverse stakeholders and to work autonomously. Strategic vision for the communication and outreach strategy of the unit's first year of activity. SELECTION COMMITTEE : Chairperson: Mariano Torcal, IP / Scientific Director SPEDD. Alternate Chairperson: Veronica Benet, guarantor. Secretary: Ainara Huarte, Project Manager, SPEDD. Alternate secretary: Esther Celma, Head of Administrative Unit. Member: Ricard Clarà, UPF communication Office Team, head of Campus Ciutadella. Alternate member: Marina Carré Molina, Pre-doctoral Researcher. Publication date: 02/10/2026 Deadline to submit applications: 16/10/2026 To apply for this position, candidates have to send their documents through Interfolio Curriculum vitae (“CV_Lastname, Name.pdf”) Cover letter (at most 1 page) explaining the reasons why the candidate is interested in this position and describing the candidate’s expertise and experience related to the requirements of this position (“Letter_Lastname, Name.pdf”) Name and contact details of 2 academic/professional referees Copy of degree level (“Degree_Lastname, Name.pdf”) A copy of ID card or passport More informartion Contact : mdm_cpis@upf.edu Link to euraxess : https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/jobs/470124 Information about the call and selection process : https://www.upf.edu/web/politiques/ofertes-de-treball/-/asset_publisher/QusHfk4KCeGQ/content/1_ref-call-cpis-psr-2026-22-full-time-communication-knowledge-transfer-manager-of-the-maria-de-maeztu-unit-of-excellence-within-the-department-of-political-and-social-sciences-at-universitat-pompeu-fabra-upf-/maximized"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194918": {
      "title": "1 PhD candidate in University of Sousse HORIZON-MSCA-2023-DN-01-01 - REF: CPIS-PREDOC-2026-04",
      "description": "Department: Pompeu Fabra University: Department of Political and Social Sciences Location: Sousse, Tunisia EuroMedMig PhD Network is funded by the Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions (Doctoral Networks), under the Call: HORIZON-MSCA-2023-DN-01-01. The PhD candidates will be incorporated in the respective PhD programmes in September 2025 for three years.  It is an initiative of EuroMedMig (Euro-Mediterranean Research Network on Migrations) – UPF, an independent interdisciplinary platform of researchers promoting multilateral knowledge production and exchange both between Universities and with Policy and Social actors. EuroMedMig PhD Network seeks to promote a sound community of leading Early-Stage Researchers (ESRs) in the field of migration and refugees in the Mediterranean region, offering a meeting point for a variety of methodologies, disciplines and levels of analysis, connecting the new generation of outstanding researchers from the South, North, East and West of the Mediterranean. The core philosophy is to promote multilateral knowledge production and exchange, with 10 partner universities and 6 associate partners from all rims of the Mediterranean, which ensures a plurality of perspectives by incorporating the Mediterranean as a regional scale of migration research with shared epistemological principles, avoiding research generalisations and knowledge-centrism, and with intercultural and humanitarian values. The main objective of EuroMedMig PhD Network is twofold: ⇒ to ensure an innovative research agenda on Mediterranean migrations for the coming years, and ⇒ to create promising avenues for further research by bringing together a community of top young researchers from all shores of the Mediterranean and a variety of topics and research lines, disciplines and methodologies. The EuroMedMig PhD network is structured around three main guiding principles Pillar 1: Promoting Research Excellence: EuroMedMig PhD Network promotes Mediterranean migration studies and seeks to be a platform of researchers sharing epistemological principles away from Eurocentrism and generalisations when researching migrations in the Mediterranean. It facilitates cross-discipline approaches, innovative policy frameworks related to Mediterranean human mobility, diversity management, integration principles, geopolitical thinking and advances migration governance frameworks. Pillar 2: Developing Advanced Training for ESRs interested in Mediterranean migration studies in the form of thematic and methodological training courses and lectures. It also seeks to develop advanced learning through interaction with policy makers, CSOs, media, consultants and experts specialised in Mediterranean Migration Studies. Pillar 3: Fostering Policy and Social Dialogues: Promoting evidence-based research and social/policy dialogue between practitioners and stakeholders, and ESRs on Mediterranean Migration challenges. This call looks at promising pioneering research projects with innovative research contributions within THEME 4 [1] : ECONOMY AND LABOUR MARKET: Mediterranean migrations have significant implications for the economy and labour markets in the region. Some key points to tentatively consider include: shaping labour market dynamics (migrants contribute to the labour force, filling gaps in various sectors and often by engaging in low-skilled or manual labour, including agriculture, construction, and domestic work), high skilled migrants working for the global Mediterranean economy, positive and negative economic impact assessment (businesses creation and entrepreneurial trans-Mediterranean ventures stimulating national/regional/local economies), so-called irregular migrants and the informal economy (this may refer to work that is not regulated, lacks social protection, and often offers low wages and poor working conditions), or successful integration of migrants into the labour market. Jobs and labour resources, including access to education, language training, and skills development programs enhancing migrants' employability, will also be considered. Policies that promote the recognition of foreign qualifications and skills can also contribute to better labour market outcomes for migrants. For further information : https://www.upf.edu/web/euromedmig-phd-network [1] The positions for Themes 1, 2 and 3 were fulfilled in a previous call. PhD Candidate 12 Research scope: Economy and Labour Markets at the Urban and Rural Interface Description: This research project seeks to decipher the interconnectedness between Economy and the Urban and Rural interface. The Rural-Urban divide needs to be assessed when analysing economic impacts linked to migration, as well as subsequent labour market restructuration. How are agricultural zones also affected by migration? Regarding agriculture and other working spheres, informal economy will also be analysed, as well as the vulnerabilities it brings to migrants working under no protection. Host institution: University of Sousse Supervisor: Hassen Boubakri ( hassen.boubakri@flsh.u-sousse.tn ) Terms and conditions of the contract: ● Institution funding the contract, title and reference of the project Organisation: Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions Doctoral Network (HORIZON-MSCA-2023-DN-01-01): - EuroMedMig PhD Network. -      REF: CPIS-PREDOC-PIPF-2026-04 - Official number reference: 101169465, European Commission - Program: Horizon Europe (2021-2027) - Research Line: Migration, Mediterranean and Governance ● Wage: wage is as stated by the European Commission for all Marie-Curie Doctoral Networks. For indicative wages, which will differ according to the country and whether the mobility or family allowance applies to the selected candidate, further indicative information can be found in the following Horizon Europe official MSCA document (please particularly check p.109 and p.140): https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/docs/2021-2027/horizon/wp-call/2023-2024/wp-2-msca-actions_horizon-2023-2024_en.pdf Bear in mind that the indicated amounts are the total recruitment costs (gross salaries + the social security coverage to be ensured by the employer), and therefore cannot be equated to gross salaries. ● Type of contract: Full-time (100%) contract as a university employee with full social security coverage. ● Job location : the DC will be required to be based at the host institutions indicated above (university of Sousse) ● The estimated starting date is January 2027 to February 2029 , with the possibility of an extension in line with any extension of the project. ● Co-supervision and Consortium Synergy Encouraged To maximize the impact and interdisciplinary nature of the research, co-supervision with other partners within the consortium will be actively encouraged and promoted for this PhD position. This approach allows the candidate to benefit from joint expertise, shared resources, cross-sectoral collaboration, and international secondments of up to 12 months at another consortium partner's institution. Impartiality principles and protocol for conflicts of interest General eligibility criteria In order to be admitted as a EuroMedMig Marie Curie PhD candidate, candidates must provide evidence that they have obtained, or will have obtained before the start of the PhD, an accredited graduate/Master’s degree in the field of Social Sciences that enables them to access a doctoral programme at the host institution. Candidates must not be in possession of a doctoral degree at the date of recruitment. Candidates who have successfully defended their doctoral thesis before the date of recruitment are also considered ineligible, even if the doctoral degree has not yet been formally awarded Candidates of any nationality are invited to apply, provided that they comply with the MSCA Doctoral Networks mobility rule . At the date of recruitment, candidates must not have resided or carried out their main activity (work, studies, etc.) in the country of the recruiting beneficiary for more than 12 months during the 36 months immediately preceding the recruitment date . In determining eligibility, periods of compulsory national service, time spent as part of a procedure for obtaining refugee status under the Geneva Convention, and short stays such as holidays are not taken into account. Selection process: The selection process will be divided into two phases: 1)      The first stage is an assessment of the candidate's application 2)      Shortlisted candidates (scoring above 70%) will be invited for a virtual interview. Application Materials and Assessment Criteria To apply for these positions, candidates must send the documentation by Interfolio through the following link: XXX The following documents are to be uploaded: ID card or passport Candidacy form (to be found in the Interfolio Platform) A copy of the undergraduate and graduate degree/diploma or certification/proof of degree completion (Bachelor degree and Master’s degree). If you have not yet completed your graduate/master's studies when formalising application, you will need to provide us with the following documents: a signed declaration of obtaining your graduate/master's degree before the commencement of the PhD programme. Combine all documents into a single PDF file (“Degrees_Lastname,Name.pdf”). A copy of the official final grade transcript, both of bachelor’s and master’s diploma . IIf the diploma or transcripts are not issued in Catalan, Spanish, English, French, Portuguese, or Italian, a sworn translation into English must also be submitted. Combine both transcripts into a single PDF file (“Grades_Lastname,Name.pdf”) CV (“CV_Lastname,Name.pdf”) Research proposal (“Proposal_Lastname,Name.pdf”) Motivation letter (“Letter_Lastname,Name.pdf”) Recommendation Letters: Applicants must provide two letters of recommendation, preferably from different universities. If both letters are from the same institution, they should come from distinct departments. Letters must be compiled into a single PDF file (“Recommendation_Lastname, Name.pdf”). Proof of English language (B2). In order to be exempt from accreditation, being English your mother tongue or having studied in that language, you must upload a brief letter justifying the reasons why you request to be exempted from this requirement. Form for Students_EuroMedMig PhD Network The following describes the main documents to be sent and evaluated, as well as their evaluation criteria: Curriculum Vitae 30% Complete CV including details of any information supporting the submission (e.g. links to papers produced during the masters’ courses, publications, participation in seminars and research debates, etc.) Research project proposal 40% Clearly indicate the position for which you are applying by ticking the appropriate box. Candidates can only apply to 1 position. The maximum length of the proposal is 3,000 words (excluding references). 1.  Provisional title of the research 2.  General literature review 3.  Research questions, aims and main theoretical framework 4.  Main innovations and contribution to migration Mediterranean studies 5.  Research design, sources and methodology 6.  Expected policy and/or societal contribution 7.  Research schedule, including planned secondments to other partner universities and associated partners. 8.  List of references Motivation Letter 20% The maximum length of the letter is 1,000 words. Candidates are encouraged to include the following information: 1) Vision for academic career in the medium and long term. 2) Expectations for the training received to contribute to the advancement of Mediterranean migration studies. 3) Brief overview of your career achievements to date. Letters of recommendation 10% Two letters of recommendation are required. In order to ensure the optimal treatment and security of the recommendation letters, it is the responsibility of the candidate to request them via the online application system. In doing so, the candidate is required to indicate the email address of the person or persons whom they wish to be recommended by. The individual in question will then receive an email notification indicating that the candidate has requested a recommendation letter from them. The referee will upload the letter to the online application system. It should be noted that addresses of a non-institutional nature, such as those ending in Yahoo, Gmail, Hotmail, and so forth, will not be accepted."
    },
