    "https://apply.interfolio.com/107232": {
      "title": "PhD position on Chimera states in mathematical models of coupled networks.",
      "description": "Department: Pompeu Fabra University: Department of Engineering Location: Universitat Pompeu Fabra, Barcelona, Spain The nonlinear time series analysis group of the Department of Information and Communication Technologies of the Universitat Pompeu Fabra, Barcelona, Spain offers a PhD position starting in November 2022. The research of the group is positioned at the interface between physics, applied mathematics, and neuroscience. The PhD project will be dedicated to the study of chimera states in mathematical models of networks of coupled oscillators or maps. For details on this line of research please see: https://www.upf.edu/web/ntsa/publications-featured . The student will receive a fellowship during three years, which can be extended to a fourth year. The contract is renewed yearly provided that sufficient progress has been made. The student will have to teach some seminars in undergraduate physics or math courses at our department. The student should have a background in physics, mathematics or related fields. The study of the networks is primarily numerical and therefore strong programming skills are required. Analytical aspects can be added, but will not be the main focus of this work. The thesis involves no laboratory or experimental work. Previous experience in the study of dynamical systems is a plus. The candidate will work in our nonlinear time series analysis group, an international team that puts a strong emphasis on well-organized supervision of its junior members and regular research activities such as journal clubs, project meetings, etc. To apply please submit a detailed motivation letter. It is recommended that this motivation letter relates to our group’s recent publications in the topic. This can be done by summarizing some aspect of this work and brainstorming on possible ideas for a project to continue this line of research. The submission should furthermore include your CV and certificates of your undergraduate studies. The candidate selected by our research group will afterwards have to formally apply to our PhD program. Details can be found here: https://www.upf.edu/web/etic/predoctoral-research-contracts Applications should be submitted as soon as possible but not later than July 1st, 2022.  You should furthermore ask two reviewers to upload a letter of recommendation to this application system."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/109386": {
      "title": "Investigador Postdoctoral en el projecte Aprendizaje y Planificación Continua PID2019-108141GB-I00",
      "description": "Department: Pompeu Fabra University: Department of Engineering Location: Universitat Pompeu Fabra, Barcelona, España El projecte de recerca es centrarà a l'aprenentatge i el descobriment de les representacions compactes que ajudin a un agent de resoldre un problema de decisió seqüencial de manera més eficient. Els problemes de decisió seqüencials, principalment en forma de l'aprenentatge per reforç (reinforcement learning), són un tipus de problema molt estudiat en la intel·ligència artificial, amb aplicacions en el món real com el control de robots, dels reactors de les centrals elèctriques, i dels sistemes de navegació. Les tasques a desenvolupar pel candidat inclouen les següents: Desenvolupar nous algorismes per a l'aprenentatge per les representacions compactes. Demostrar les propietats teòriques dels algorismes desenvolupats usant les eines matemàtiques. Implementar aquests algorismes en un llenguatge de programació. Realitzar experiments i simulacions amb els algorismes en els dominis estàndard. Escriure articles i presentar el treball en els congressos internacionals. Es podrà assignar docència, eventualment, fins a un màxim de 60h anuals dins la jornada laboral. 1. Formació Acadèmica: 0-20 punts. 2. Experiència professional/Adequació al perfil proposat: 0-60 punts. 3. Altres mèrits: 0-20 punts. La puntuació mínima per a superar el procés de selecció és: 80 punts. a) Tenir la nacionalitat espanyola o ser nacional d’algun dels Estats membres de la Unió Europea. En cas de tenir nacionalitat extracomunitària, la formalització del contracte quedarà subjecte a l’obtenció del permís de treball d’acord amb la Llei orgànica 4/2000, d’11 de gener, sobre drets i llibertats dels estrangers a Espanya i la seva integració social i disposicions reglamentàries d’aplicació. b) Tenir la capacitat funcional per al desenvolupament de les tasques objecte del contracte. c) No haver estat separat mitjançant expedient disciplinari del servei de cap de les administracions públiques, ni trobar-se inhabilitat per sentència ferma per al desenvolupament de les funcions públiques. En el cas de ser nacional d’un altre Estat, no trobar-se inhabilitat o en situació equivalent ni haver estat sotmès a sanció disciplinària o equivalent que impedeixi, en el seu Estat, en els mateixos termes l’accés a llocs de treball públics. d) Estar en possessió del títol de Doctor. En el cas que el títol no hagi estat expedit per una universitat espanyola o reconegut en el país, per signar el contracte ha d’haver estat declarat equivalent a nivell acadèmic de doctor. https://seuelectronica.upf.edu/declaracio-equivalencia-doctor Aquests requisits de participació s’han de complir el darrer dia de termini per presentar sol·licituds, s’han de poder acreditar fefaentment en qualsevol moment del procés selectiu i s'han de continuar complint en la data de signatura de contracte."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/115289": {
      "title": "Professors Associats en Tecnologia (2ª crida)",
      "description": "Department: Pompeu Fabra University: Department of Engineering Location: Barcelona Crida extraordinària del Departament de Tecnologies de la Informació i les Comunicacions de la UPF per omplir fins a 20 places de Professors Associats a temps parcial per via d’urgència en diverses assignatures, amb una remuneració de 70 EUR / hora (bruts). La data límit per aplicar és el 25 d'octubre de 2022. Per qualsevol dubte, si us plau contacteu amb sotsdireccio.docenciadtic@upf.edu – English version – The Department of Information and Communication Technologies at UPF opens an extraordinary call for Assistant Professors, with part-time urgent hiring of up to 20 positions in several subjects. The raw salary is at a rate of 70 EUR / hour. Applications are accepted till 25-10-2022. For informal queries, please contact with: sotsdireccio.docenciadtic@upf.edu Per aplicar, cal aportar: currículum actualitzat informe de vida laboral especificar l'assignatura per la qual es postula, d'acord amb el llistat següent: Càlcul II Fonaments de Física Estructures de Dades i Algorismes I Estructures de Dades i Algorismes II Organització de Computadors Mètodes Numèrics Estadística Sistemes Operatius Disseny d'Algorismes Sistemes Distribuïts de Gran Escala Introduccio a la Programació Programació Objectes – English version – Applicants must provide: an updated copy of their CV a certificate of work experience, clearly indicating the subject to which they wish to apply, according to the list below: Calculus II Foundations of Physics Data Structures and Algorithms I Data Structures and Algorithms II Computer Organization Numerical Methods Statistics Operating Systems Algorithm Design Large-scale Distributed Systems Introduction to Programming Object-Oriented Programming"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/127072": {
      "title": "Investigador Post doc  -  Teoria de la informació amb lleis incertes",
      "description": "Department: Pompeu Fabra University: Department of Engineering Location: Barcelona Realització d'activitats cientificotècniques en la línia de recerca en teoria de la informació amb lleis incertes Aquest projecte té com a objectiu contribuir a l'ambiciós objectiu de proporcionar un marc unificat per a l'estudi de la teoria de la informació amb lleis incertes. Es desenvoluparà un marc general basat en la prova d'hipòtesis i es derivaran dissenys i construccions de codi que es deriven naturalment de la formulació de la prova d'hipòtesis. Aquest tractament no convencional i desafiant de la Teoria de la Informació farà avançar l'àrea i contribuirà a les disciplines de Ciències de la Informació i Sistemes on la Teoria de la Informació és rellevant. Com a part del projecte, l’investigador estudiarà varis aspects de la teoria de la informació com ara test d’hipotesis, exponents d’error, aproximacions saddlepoint, cotes de capacitat i decodificació mismatched. Un estudi exhaustiu dels límits fonamentals i el disseny de codi òptim segons lleis d’incertesa per als models generals representarà un gran pas endavant en el camp, amb el potencial de proporcionar noves eines i tècniques per resoldre problemes oberts en disciplines properes. Per tant, els resultats d'aquest projecte no només beneficiaran les comunicacions, sinó també àrees com la teoria de la probabilitat, l'estadística, la física, la informàtica i l'economia. Recercador senior experimentat ( més de 15 any de recerca post doc) a) Tenir la nacionalitat espanyola o ser nacional d’algun dels Estats membres de la Unió Europea. En cas de tenir nacionalitat extracomunitària, la formalització del contracte quedarà subjecte a l’obtenció del permís de treball d’acord amb la Llei orgànica 4/2000, d’11 de gener, sobre drets i llibertats dels estrangers a Espanya i la seva integració social i disposicions reglamentàries d’aplicació. b) Tenir la capacitat funcional per al desenvolupament de les tasques objecte del contracte. c) No haver estat separat mitjançant expedient disciplinari del servei de cap de les administracions públiques, ni trobar-se inhabilitat per sentència ferma per al desenvolupament de les funcions públiques. En el cas de ser nacional d’un altre Estat, no trobar-se inhabilitat o en situació equivalent ni haver estat sotmès a sanció disciplinària o equivalent que impedeixi, en el seu Estat, en els mateixos termes l’accés a llocs de treball públics. d) Estar en possessió del títol de Doctor En el cas que el títol no hagi estat expedit per una universitat espanyola o reconegut en el país, per signar el contracte ha d’haver estat declarat equivalent a nivell acadèmic de doctor. https://seuelectronica.upf.edu/declaracio-equivalencia-doctor ESPECÍFICS - Experiència en direcció de projectes en teoria de la informació - Experiència en supervisió de doctorands in investigadors - Experiència en publicació en les millors revistes d’àmbit internacional (IEEE Transactions on Information Theory) - Experiència en servei a la comunitat internacional (editor, organització de congressos,...) Idiomes requerits ( nivell nadiu) Català, Castellà, Anglès Requeriments addicionals: - Experiència en direcció de projectes en teoria de la informació - Experiència en supervisió de doctorands in investigadors - Experiència en publicació en les millors revistes d’àmbit internacional (IEEE Transactions on Information Theory) - Experiència en servei a la comunitat internacional (editor, organització de congressos,...) A través d'Interfolio"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190955": {
      "title": "PhD Position 1 (PhD1): Multisensory Prosody in Spoken Catalan (TRAD-PREDOCTORAL-2026-02)",
      "description": "Department: Pompeu Fabra University: Department of Translation and Language Sciences Location: Barcelona Note: This page is for informative purposes only. The official call (particularly, the legal requirements for candidates) and all information related to the selection process (admission, short list, final result) is published in the Department’s website. Position description: The Prosodic and Gestural Studies Research Group (GREPG) in the Department of Translation and Language Sciences at Universitat Pompeu Fabra (UPF) invites applications for a fully funded PhD position within the ERC Advanced Grant PROSODY-SENSES: Prosody across senses: Testing a reconceptualization of prosody as a modality-neutral component of language governing spoken, visual and tactile signals , led by Prof. Pilar Prieto. PhD1: Multisensory Prosody in Spoken Catalan The successful candidate will contribute to Strand 1 of the project, investigating the multisensory implementation of prosody in spoken Catalan. The project will examine how prominence and grouping are jointly realized through speech, facial movements, head movements, manual gestures, and hand pressure signals. Drawing on controlled production experiments and multimodal corpora, the candidate will combine acoustic, kinematic, and linguistic analyses with three-dimensional motion capture to investigate modality-neutral principles of prosodic organization. The candidate will contribute to the development of annotation protocols and quantitative analyses for modelling the magnitude and temporal coordination of prosodic cues across speech data, working closely with the ERC postdoctoral researcher responsible for multimodal motion-capture modelling. The dissertation will follow an article-based format, comprising three to four publishable papers in international peer-reviewed journals. The candidate will be jointly supervised by Dr. Patrick L. Rohrer (Universitat Rovira i Virgili) and Prof. Pilar Prieto (ICREA–Universitat Pompeu Fabra), and will also benefit from close co-supervision and methodological training provided by one of the ERC-funded postdoctoral researchers specializing in multimodal motion-capture modelling. Together, this supervisory team will provide complementary expertise in multimodal communication, prosody, and advanced motion-capture methodologies. Tasks: Design and conduct experimental studies on the multisensory production of prosody in Catalan. Collect multimodal datasets using synchronized audio-video recording and optical motion capture. Annotate and analyse acoustic, facial, head, and manual movement data. Contribute to the development of quantitative models of multimodal prosodic coordination. Publish research articles in leading international journals. Present results at international conferences. Participate actively in project meetings, seminars, workshops, and dissemination activities. Contribute to collaborative activities within the ERC project. Eligibility Applicants must: Hold (or be close to completing) a Master's degree in Linguistics, Experimental Phonetics, Cognitive Science, Neuroscience, Psychology, Computer Science, Biomedical Engineering, or a closely related discipline. Demonstrate strong interest in speech/multisensory prosody, multimodal communication, language production, or experimental phonetics. Have experience with experimental research and quantitative data analysis. Have previous experience writing scientific articles or conference papers. Demonstrate excellent teamwork and communication skills. Have excellent written and spoken English. Native or near-native proficiency in Catalan is strongly preferred, as the project involves the collection and analysis of Catalan spoken language. Experience with motion capture, audiovisual annotation, ELAN, Praat, R, or Python Academic excellence and previous research experience (40%) Quality and relevance of Master's thesis and previous publications (25%) Fit with the scientific objectives of PROSODY-SENSES (20%) Personal interview, during which the candidate's motivation, communication skills, research potential, knowledge of the research area, ability to work collaboratively, and overall fit with the project and its interdisciplinary research environment will be assessed (15%). Candidates obtaining at least 75/100 on the first three points may be invited for an interview. Applicants should submit the following documents: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Academic transcripts (Bachelor's and Master's) Copy of MA or MSc degree (or expected completion certificate) One writing sample (published paper, Master's thesis chapter, or equivalent) Contact details of two academic referees Copy of passport or national identity card"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190956": {
      "title": "PhD Position 2 (PhD2): Multisensory Prosody in Spoken Portuguese  (TRAD-PREDOCTORAL-2026-03)",
      "description": "Department: Pompeu Fabra University: Department of Translation and Language Sciences Location: Barcelona Note: This page is for informative purposes only. The official call (particularly, the legal requirements for candidates) and all information related to the selection process (admission, short list, final result) is published in the Department’s website. Position description: The Prosodic and Gestural Studies Research Group (GREPG) in the Department of Translation and Language Sciences at Universitat Pompeu Fabra (UPF) invites applications for a fully funded PhD position within the ERC Advanced Grant PROSODY-SENSES: Prosody across senses: Testing a reconceptualization of prosody as a modality-neutral component of language governing spoken, visual and tactile signals , led by Prof. Pilar Prieto. Multisensory Prosody in Spoken European Portuguese The successful candidate will contribute to Strand 1 of the project, investigating the multisensory implementation of prosody in spoken European Portuguese. The project will examine how prominence and grouping are jointly realized through speech, facial movements, head movements, manual gestures, and hand pressure signals. Drawing on controlled production experiments and multimodal corpora, the candidate will combine acoustic, kinematic, and linguistic analyses with three-dimensional motion capture to investigate modality-neutral principles of prosodic organization. The candidate will contribute to the development of annotation protocols and quantitative analyses for modelling the magnitude and temporal coordination of prosodic cues across speech data, working closely with the ERC postdoctoral researcher responsible for multimodal motion-capture modelling. The dissertation will follow an article-based format, comprising three to four publishable papers in international peer-reviewed journ als. The PhD will be carried out under a cotutelle agreement between the University of Lisbon and the Universitat Pompeu Fabra. The candidate will be jointly supervised by Prof. Sónia Frota and Dr. Marisa Cruz (University of Lisbon) and Prof. Pilar Prieto (ICREA–Universitat Pompeu Fabra), ensuring close integration between the two institutions throughout the doctoral training. Th e cotutelle arrangement will provide complementary expertise in spoken language prosody, multimodal communication, and cross-modal linguistic theory, while giving the candidate access to the research infrastructure, training opportunities, and academic environments of both universities. In addition, the candidate will receive close scientific guidance from two ERC-funded postdoctoral researchers specializing in multimodal motion-capture modelling, who will provide mentorship and methodological expertise throughout the project. Tasks: Design and conduct experimental studies on the multisensory production of prosody in European Portuguese . Collect multimodal datasets using synchronized audio-video recording and optical motion capture. Annotate and analyze acoustic, facial, head, and manual and non-manual movement data. Contribute to the development of quantitative models of multimodal prosodic coordination. Publish research articles in leading international journals. Present results at international conferences. Participate actively in project meetings, seminars, workshops, and dissemination activities. Contribute to collaborative activities within the ERC project. Eligibility Applicants must: Hold (or be close to completing) a Master's degree in Linguistics, Experimental Phonetics, Cognitive Science, Neuroscience, Psychology, Computer Science, Biomedical Engineering, or a closely related discipline. Demonstrate strong interest in speech/multisensory prosody, multimodal communication, language production, or experimental phonetics. Have experience with experimental research and quantitative data analysis. Have previous experience writing scientific articles or conference papers. Demonstrate excellent teamwork and communication skills. Native or near-native proficiency in (European) Portuguese is strongly preferred, as the project involves the collection and analysis of Portuguese spoken language. Have excellent written and spoken English. As the PhD will be conducted in English, previous knowledge of Catalan and Portuguese is not required. However, the successful candidate is expected to begin learning Catalan and Portuguese as soon as possible and actively participate in the local research environment at UPF and U Lisbon respectively. Experience with motion capture, audiovisual annotation, ELAN, Praat, R, or Python will be considered an advantage. Academic excellence and previous research experience (40%) Quality and relevance of Master's thesis and previous publications (25%) Fit with the scientific objectives of PROSODY-SENSES (20%) Personal interview, during which the candidate's motivation, communication skills, research potential, knowledge of the research area, ability to work collaboratively, and overall fit with the project and its interdisciplinary research environment will be assessed (15%). Candidates obtaining at least 75/100 on the first three points may be invited for an interview. Applicants should submit the following documents: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Academic transcripts (Bachelor's and Master's) Copy of MA or MSc degree (or expected completion certificate) One writing sample (published paper, Master's thesis chapter, or equivalent) Contact details of two academic referees Copy of passport or national identity card"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190957": {
      "title": "PhD Position 6: Multisensory Prosody in Portuguese Sign Language (TRAD-PREDOCTORAL-2026-04)",
      "description": "Department: Pompeu Fabra University: Department of Translation and Language Sciences Location: Barcelona Note: This page is for informative purposes only. The official call (particularly, the legal requirements for candidates) and all information related to the selection process (admission, short list, final result) is published in the Department’s website. Position description: The Prosodic and Gestural Studies Research Group (GREPG) in the Department of Translation and Language Sciences at Universitat Pompeu Fabra (UPF) invites applications for a fully funded PhD position within the ERC Advanced Grant PROSODY-SENSES: Prosody across senses: Testing a reconceptualization of prosody as a modality-neutral component of language governing spoken, visual and tactile signals , led by Prof. Pilar Prieto. PhD6: Multisensory Prosody in European Portuguese Sign Language The successful candidate will contribute to Strand 2 of the project, investigating the multisensory implementation of prosody in Portuguese Sign Language (Língua Gestual Portuguesa, LGP). The project will examine how prominence, grouping, and other prosodic functions are realized across spoken and sign language modalities through speech, facial expressions, head and body movements, and manual and non-manual articulations. Drawing on controlled production experiments and multimodal corpora, the candidate will combine kinematic, and linguistic analyses with three-dimensional motion capture to investigate modality-neutral principles of prosodic organization. The candidate will contribute to the development of annotation protocols and quantitative analyses for modelling the magnitude and temporal coordination of prosodic cues across speech and sign, working closely with the ERC postdoctoral researcher responsible for multimodal motion-capture modelling. The dissertation will follow an article-based format, comprising three to four publishable papers in international peer-reviewed journ als. The PhD will be carried out under a cotutelle agreement between the University of Lisbon and the Universitat Pompeu Fabra. The candidate will be jointly supervised by Prof. Sónia Frota and Dr. Marisa Cruz (University of Lisbon) and Prof. Pilar Prieto (ICREA–Universitat Pompeu Fabra), ensuring close integration between the two institutions throughout the doctoral training. Th e cotutelle arrangement will provide complementary expertise in sign language prosody, multimodal communication, and cross-modal linguistic theory, while giving the candidate access to the research infrastructure, training opportunities, and academic environments of both universities. In addition, the candidate will receive close scientific guidance from two ERC-funded postdoctoral researchers specializing in multimodal motion-capture modelling, who will provide mentorship and methodological expertise throughout the project. Tasks: Design and conduct experimental studies on the multisensory production of prosody in Portuguese Sign Language (Língua Gestual Portuguesa, LGP). Collect multimodal datasets using synchronized audio-video recording and optical motion capture. Annotate and analyze facial, head, and manual and non-manual movement data. Contribute to the development of quantitative models of multimodal prosodic coordination in sign languages. Publish research articles in leading international journals. Present results at international conferences. Participate actively in project meetings, seminars, workshops, and dissemination activities. Contribute to collaborative activities within the ERC project. Eligibility Applicants must: Hold (or be close to completing) a Master's degree in Linguistics, Experimental Phonetics, Cognitive Science, Neuroscience, Psychology, Computer Science, Biomedical Engineering, or a closely related discipline. Demonstrate strong interest in multisensory prosody, multimodal communication, language production, or experimental phonetics. Have experience with experimental research and quantitative data analysis. Have previous experience writing scientific articles or conference papers. Demonstrate excellent teamwork and communication skills. Demonstrate knowledge of Portuguese Sign Language or possibly another sign language, as the project involves the collection and analysis of Portuguese Sign Language data. Have excellent written and spoken English. As the PhD will be conducted in English, previous knowledge of Catalan is not required. However, the successful candidate is expected to begin learning Catalan and Portuguese as soon as possible and actively participate in the local research environment at UPF and U Lisbon respectively. Experience with motion capture, audiovisual annotation, ELAN, R, or Python will be considered an advantage. Academic excellence and previous research experience (40%) Quality and relevance of Master's thesis and previous publications (25%) Fit with the scientific objectives of PROSODY-SENSES (20%) Personal interview, during which the candidate's motivation, communication skills, research potential, knowledge of the research area, ability to work collaboratively, and overall fit with the project and its interdisciplinary research environment will be assessed (15%). Candidates obtaining at least 75/100 on the first three points may be invited for an interview. Applicants should submit the following documents: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Academic transcripts (Bachelor's and Master's) Copy of MSc degree (or expected completion certificate) One writing sample (published paper, Master's thesis chapter, or equivalent) Contact details of two academic referees Copy of passport or national identity card"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194495": {
      "title": "ENG-PSR-CAC-2026-36 - 2 Specialist support technicians in Biomedical Engineering",
      "description": "Department: Pompeu Fabra University: Department of Engineering - PSR Location: BARCELONA - Universitat Pompeu Fabra Project description: The Biomedical Electronics Research Group (BERG) at Universitat Pompeu Fabra is a research team who has been awarded the European Innovation Council (EIC) Transition grant for the project FORESEE. The project is meant to develop and validate an innovative microsensing platform for remote monitoring of heart failure patients. The platform consists of a sensor embedded in an active implantable medical device and a portable external system to wirelessly power and communicate with it. Line of research: Active implantable medical devices (Biomedical Engineering) Tasks to be performed: Scientific-technical activities and scientific-technical management related to the activities of the FORESEE project, including: • Prototyping: CAD design (Fusion 360/FreeCAD). • Development of computational simulations (finite element methods, SPICE) related to the project and analysis of results (e.g., Ansys fluid, COMSOL Multiphysics). • Use of MATLAB, C++ and Python. • Contact with suppliers and manufacturers of parts of implantable devices. • Search and analysis of devices made by competing companies, and tracking of components they use. • Research and analysis of technologies and methods used in implantable devices manufacturing and industrialization. • Research and analysis of other market opportunities where the technology could have an impact. • Preparation and participation in discussions with stakeholders about injectable technology. • Participation in analysis of pre-clinical studies, including bench testing and animal experiments. • Drafting of documentation. The duration of these tasks is estimated over a period of 5 months. Group and complement: Grup 3 + Nivell p-u based on experience and skills. Dedication and working hours: Part time (15 h/week). Planned remuneration approx: 13.265,34 –14.012,70 €  gross per year based on your experience and skills (956,26 € - 1.018,57 € gross monthly). Financing fund: ● PREUR02623 - EC-HEu-101136633-EIT-FORESEE (Novel microsensing platform for remote patient monitoring Grant 101136633 funded by the European Union) ● RECEU01022 - RECERCA EUROPA Requirements: High school-FP2 The expected start date is December 1st, 2026, the job is in Barcelona. Selection criteria: The selection of the candidates will be made through evaluation of the curriculum and, where appropriate, with the carrying out a test and/or interview. Valuation will be as follows: 1- Academic Training (0-30 points). ● BSc. Biomedical Engineering 2- Other professional training and experience, adequacy to the proposed profile (0-50 points): ● Experience in supporting research activities. ● Experience on finite element method and SPICE simulations. ● Good communication skills. ● Experience in searching for materials and literature review. ● Experience in data analysis obtained from pre-clinical studies. 3- Other merits (0-20 points): ● Languages: English, Spanish (Catalan will be considered very positively) The minimum score to pass the selection process is 85 points. The candidate with the highest score in the selection process will be offered the job. BASIC INFORMATION ON DATA PROTECTION: Data Controller: Universitat Pompeu Fabra Purpose: Research support staff recruitment. Rights: You can access your data; request their rectification, deletion and portability; you may object to their processing and request their limitation. Additional information: Further detailed information is available on the website: https://rat.upf.edu/ca/ll040"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194671": {
      "title": "ENG-PSR-CAC-2026-37 Research support position - Specialist support technician",
      "description": "Department: Pompeu Fabra University: Department of Engineering - PSR Location: BARCELONA - Universitat Pompeu Fabra Descripció del projecte/ Project description : The research assistant will join a multidisciplinary project team led by Nuria Sebastian, director of the Speech Acquisition and Perception lab, https://www.upf.edu/web/sap, Center for Brain and Cognition, https://www.upf.edu/web/cbc,  Pompeu Fabra University.  The position is supported by Grant PID2024-155658NB-I00 funded by MICIU/AEI/10.13039/501100011033 and by “ERDF A way of making Europe” The research aims at exploring the impact of language distance in early (simultaneous) bilingualism on fundamental processes of speech perception. To this end we plan to test a diverse sample of simultaneous bilinguals in adulthood. / L'assistent de recerca s'incorporarà a un equip de projecte multidisciplinari liderat per Nuria Sebastian, directora del laboratori d'adquisició i percepció de la parla, https://www.upf.edu/web/sap, Center for Brain and Cognition, https://www.upf.edu/web/cbc, Universitat Pompeu Fabra. El suport es PID2024-155658NB-I00  MICIU/AEI/10.13039/501100011033 i  “ERDF A way of making Europe” La  investigació pretén explorar l'impacte de la distància lingüística en el bilingüisme precoç (simultani) en els processos fonamentals de percepció de la parla. Amb aquesta finalitat, tenim previst estudiar una mostra diversa de bilingües simultanis en l'edat adulta. Funció a desenvolupar/ Tasks to be performed: L'auxiliar de recerca: • Assistència en la recollida de dades d'EEG • Preprocessament d'EEG • Suport en anàlisis estadístiques • Assistència en la redacció d'articles / The research assistant: • Assist with EEG data collection • EEG preprocessing • Support in statistical analyses • Assist with article writing La durada d'aquestes tasques s'estima en un període de 12 mesos./ The duration of these tasks is estimated over a period of 12 months Retribució prevista aproximada/ Planned remuneration approx: 14.990,12€ brut per any/ 14.990,12€ gross per year Grup i complement/ Group and complement: Grup 3 + Nivell U/ Group 3 + Level U Dedicació i jornada/ Dedication and working hours: Temps parcial (17.5 h/setmana)/ part time (17.5 h/week). Fons de finançament/ Financing fund : PRESP04925 - PID2024-155658NB-I00 - Sebastian, Núria Institució : MCIN/AEI i FEDER, UE Requisits/ Requirements: ● Batxillerat-FP2/ High school-FP2. La data prevista d'inici és el  2 de novembre 2026, la feina és a Barcelona./ The expected start date is 2 November 2026, the job is in Barcelona. Criteris de selecció/ Selection criteria: La selecció dels candidats es farà mitjançant valoració del currículum i, si escau, amb la realització d’una prova i/o entrevista. La valoració serà la següent:/ The selection of the candidates will be made through evaluation of the curriculum and, where appropriate, with the carrying out a test and/or interview. Valuation will be as follows: La puntuació mínima per passar el procés de selecció és de 70 punts. La persona candidata que hagi obtingut la puntuació més alta en el procés de selecció serà l’adjudicatària del lloc de treball./ The minimum score to pass the selection process is 70 points. The candidate with the highest score in the selection process will be offered the job. 1. Formació acadèmica (0-40 punts). - Grau en Psicologia o similar. - Màster en Neurociència Cognitiva o similar. 2. Altra formació i experiència professional, adequació al perfil proposat (0-40 punts) - Experiència en un laboratori de neurociència cognitiva - Experiència en la recollida i anàlisi de dades d'EEG. 3. Altres mèrits (0-20 punts) - Bons coneixements de MATLAB i Python - Coneixements avançats d’estadística - Nivell alt d'anglès i de castellà i/o català - Capacitat de comunicació acadèmica oral i escrita - Pot començar novembre de 2026. Minimum punts: 70 / 1.         Academic Training (0-40 points) - Undergraduate degree in Psychology or similar. - Master in Cognitive Neuroscience or similar. 2.         Other professional training and experience, adequacy to the proposed profile (0-40 points): - Experience in a Cognitive Neuroscience Lab - Experience with EEG data collection and analysis. 3.         Other merits (0-20 punts): BASIC INFORMATION ON DATA PROTECTION: Data Controller: Universitat Pompeu Fabra Purpose: Research support staff recruitment. Rights: You can access your data; request their rectification, deletion and portability; you may object to their processing and request their limitation. Additional information: Further detailed information is available on the website: https://rat.upf.edu/ca/ll040"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194919": {
      "title": "ENG-PSR-CAC-2026-38 - Specialist support technician",
      "description": "Department: Pompeu Fabra University: Department of Engineering - PSR Location: BARCELONA - Universitat Pompeu Fabra Project description: The area of Biomechanics & Mechanobiology (SIMBIOSys-BMMB) of the research unit BCN MedTech, at the Department of Communication and Information Technologies (DTIC) of the University Pompeu Fabra (UPF) offers a one-year research support position, in the context of the European Research Council Consolidator Grant (ERC CoG) O-Health (101044828). The successful candidate will continue the development of an existing  systems biology model of articular cartilage regulation in healthy and osteoarthritic knee joints. The spatial mapping of cell-cell communications will be targeted, considering the cascade of events and feedback loops between synovitis and articular cartilage damage over time, and the model will be fed with patient -omics data. Main research field: Computational Biomechanics and Systems Biology Tasks to be performed: Validate, with experimental cell culture data, a coupled systems biology - finite element multiscale model that simulates the collective regulation of articular cartilage chondrocyte regulation, at the tissue level (RP1) Extensive review of the biological literature and databases, to strengthen the validation of chondrocytes mechano-sensitive regulatory network models through falsification tests (RP1) Generate a web-friendly simulator of the validated regulatory model, by using SBML standard (RP2) Exploit the multiscale model to interpret the impact of synovitis on the articular cartilage, in the lights of clinical data, by integrating proteomics measurements of patient’s synovial fluids (RP3) Group and complement: Group 3 + Level u Dedication and working hours: Part time (30 h/week) Planned remuneration approx: 25691.12 € / gross per year Financing fund: ERC Consolidator Grant O-Health (ERC-2021-COG-101044828) BASIC INFORMATION ON DATA PROTECTION: Data Controller: Universitat Pompeu Fabra Purpose: Research support staff recruitment. Rights: You can access your data; request their rectification, deletion and portability; you may object to their processing and request their limitation. Additional information: Further detailed information is available on the website: https://rat.upf.edu/ca/ll040"
    }
  },
